# kex: no-check
# `!` mutating calls only work on a plain variable binding, since the
# point is to rebind it; a non-variable receiver is a runtime error. The
# checker refuses it first (spec/error_bang_on_non_variable.kex, KEXET-0495);
# unchecked, the walker still stops at the call.
main do
  IO.printLine("before")
  [1, 2, 3].push!(4)
end
